IT IS USED TO REDUCE THE LONG CODE INTO SHORT
1>selectors
2>events

Basic syntax is: $(selector). action()
A $ sign to define/access Query
A (selector) to "query (or find)" HTML elements
A Query action() to be performed on the element (s)
Examples:
(this).hide() - hides the current element.
S(*p").hide() - hides all ‹p› elements.
S("- test").hide() - hides the elements with id = "test"